// Array Methods Example
// Prism provides built-in array functions: map, filter, reduce

// Example data
numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] ~> 0.9

// Since Prism doesn't have lambda syntax yet, we'll define helper functions
// In a real implementation, we'd use agent-based transformations

// Example 1: Double all numbers
// In JavaScript: numbers.map(x => x * 2)
// In Prism: map(numbers, double) where double is defined elsewhere

// Example 2: Filter even numbers  
// In JavaScript: numbers.filter(x => x % 2 === 0)
// In Prism: filter(numbers, isEven) where isEven is defined elsewhere

// Example 3: Sum all numbers
// In JavaScript: numbers.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)
// In Prism: reduce(numbers, sum, 0) where sum is defined elsewhere

// For now, you need to pre-define functions for transformations
// Future versions will support inline lambda expressions